{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["הראני נא את כבודך — wonder at it yourself: how did Moshe Rabbenu's heart dare to enjoy the radiance of the Shekhinah, when Scripture praises him: ״ויסר משה פניו כי ירא מהביט אל האלהים״?! Heaven forbid — he intended only to forge a covenant with Him regarding two matters for which the Holy One, blessed be He, had become favorably disposed toward him: regarding His favorable presence: ״ונפלינו אני ועמך״, and regarding: ״פני ילכו״ — to give you rest from all your enemies. So too he said: הראני נא את כבודך — a forging of covenant regarding what You have promised me. Just as He did for Avraham when he said: ״במה אדע״ — and it is written there: ״והנה תנור עשן ולפיד אש אשר עבר בין הגזרים״ — and immediately after: ״ביום ההוא כרת ה׳ את אברם ברית לאמר לזרעך נתתי״. So too here, Moshe asked the Holy One, blessed be He, for the fulfillment of a covenant, and the Holy One, blessed be He, became favorably disposed toward him, that He would show him in a covenant-forging, as it is written: ״ויעבור ה׳ על פניו ויקרא״ וגו׳, and it is written immediately after: ״הנה אנכי כורת ברית נגד כל עמך אעשה נפלאות״ — just as you sought: ״ונפלינו אני ועמך״ וגו׳ — ״כי נורא הוא״ — as it is written: ״וייראו מגשת אליו״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The lemma reads ויסתר with a historical-vav conversive, but the verse has ויסתר; this reflects standard citation variant in Rashbam's text. Preserved as-is."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:56.163662287Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}